  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (e.g., after 72+ peaks, cap next 3 days at 10% below peak).",
    "Adjust downward bias when sentiment history includes negative sentiment (e.g., >0.00 sentiment shifts to -0.25 or higher).",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if 3 consecutive forecasts are above 70.00, reduce by 0.5–1.0 per day until convergence.",
    "For 30-day horizon, reduce forecast volatility when sentiment is neutral (0.00) — smooth out extremes by 10–15%.",
    "If true outcome drops below 60.00 after 5+ consecutive days above 70.00, reduce forecast by 2–3% per day to avoid overcorrection lag.",
    "When sentiment history shows increasing negativity (e.g., -0.25 → 0.00 → 0.50), reduce forecast slope by 10–20% to reflect weakening momentum."
  ]
}
